<h2>A Smart Base While You Plan a Home</h2>
<p>Many of our readers rent in central Houston while they save for or plan a new home build. A location like this can be a smart base: you get a short commute while you build up savings and figure out which neighborhood you eventually want to own in. If you are starting to think about land and lots, read our guide to <a href="/choosing-the-right-location-for-your-texas-dream-home/">choosing the right location for your Texas home</a>, and when you are ready to understand local rules, see <a href="/understanding-building-codes-in-houston-tx-what-you-need-to-know/">building codes in Houston</a>.</p>
<p>Renting close in also gives you a feel for what matters day to day. Do you use the park constantly? Do you want a garage? Do you miss a yard? Write those observations down; they become your wish list when you sit down to plan a floor plan.</p>

<h2>Touring Checklist for Allure Hermann Park</h2>
<ul>
